# Runtime dependencies of the hosted image (Dockerfile). Only what the serving code imports: Django and its password
# hasher, the WSGI server, numpy/pandas (score store, untapped) and shapely (area geometry, imported lazily).
# geopandas, pyogrio, pyproj and requests build the stores on the laptop and are deliberately not in the image.
#
# Compile the hashed lock on Linux (CI or a build box), then commit it next to this file:
#   uv pip compile requirements.linux.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 --python-platform linux \
#       --no-header -o requirements.linux.lock
# The Dockerfile installs it with --require-hashes --no-deps, so every wheel is pinned by sha256.
